iterations.reply:
I left out the two operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm`, so it has no file or HTTP capability. Adding a log write or a fetch to `metadata.internal.example` would need a new grant, and sending customer text to that URL would also send it outside the node's authority. Logging and enrichment belong in the host or in a node that is explicitly granted those capabilities.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{customer-query, moderated-query, policy-violation, escalation-request, moderation-result};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: customer-query) -> moderation-result;
}
```

